I highly doubt you pronounce it as {brgyn}, as that is "Brrrrr gun"
(ignoring syllable length). As far as {brgn} is concerned, syllabic
consonants for me are half-ebu syllables. (Syllabic r, for example, is "er"
with a very short e.) So, I say {brgn} the same way I say {bergen}, just
quicker, which funnily enough actually makes the stress more pronounced.

